freedreno: drop draws, blits and submits only after real GPU OOM

Gate every OOM skip guard on explicit per-device/per-resource/per-variant
OOM markers set only when GPU allocation actually fails (bo_new(),
fd_bo_heap_alloc(), realloc_bo(), upload_shader_variant(),
fd_ringbuffer_sp_init()/grow()), so resources or shader variants whose
BO is NULL for any non-OOM reason take the upstream path unchanged.

Also fixes two bugs in the previous OOM patch:
- Zero-initialize emit.hs/emit.ds/emit.gs in fd6_draw.cc:draw_vbos()
  so PIPELINE == NO_TESS_GS never inspects uninitialized stack pointers.
- Track upload_failed on struct ir3_shader_variant and check it in
  ir3_cache_lookup() / fd6_draw.cc / fd6_compute.cc rather than
  returning NULL from ir3_shader_variant() or skipping solely on !bo.

Logs skip reason, OOM marker count, and skip count via mesa_loge +
sweet_drm_log once on first OOM skip in a process and via an atexit
summary if multiple skips occur before exit.

